chapter.v:
And Moses 


said to, 


his father-in-law, “Because the people come to me to inquire of God;

Moreover, look 


for able, 


men from all the people, men who fear God, who are trustworthy and hate a bribe, and place such men over the people as chiefs of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens.

Then Moses 


let his, 


father-in-law depart, and he went away to his own country. Footnotes (1) 18:3 *Gershom* sounds like the Hebrew for *sojourner* (2) 18:4 *Eliezer* means *My God is help* (3) 18:6 Hebrew; Samaritan, Septuagint, Syriac *behold* (4) 18:11 Hebrew *with them* (ESV)
